<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pact of Steel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">22 May 1939</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as Pact of Friendship and Alliance between Germany and Italy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pact of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">Steel</a> was a military and political alliance between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fascist-italy">Fascist Italy</a> and Nazi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, signed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> on 22 May 1939 by the foreign ministers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galeazzo-ciano">Galeazzo Ciano</a> and Joachim von Ribbentrop. It bound each country to support the other with all its forces in any war. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, unprepared, stayed out when Germany invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> in September 1939 and entered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> only in June 1940.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pact-of-steel.jpg" alt="Pact of Steel" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patto-acciaio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
